S4 global counts
  ok   r_4(n) = (r_2 additively convolved with r_2)(n) = 8 sigma(n) for odd n <= 400
  ok   bicomplex norm |z1|^2 |z2|^2 = n on Z[i]^2: the multiplicative convolution of r_2 with itself; it is 0 for every n = 3 (mod 4), n <= 400; values at 1, 5, 9, 13, 25: [16, 64, 32, 64, 160]
  ok   Hurwitz order: 24 sigma(n) elements of norm n for odd n < 60 (one third on the Lipschitz grid)
  ok   r_8(n) = 16 sigma_3(n) for odd n <= 39
  ok   r_8(2) = 112 is not 16 sigma_3(2) = 144 (the prime 2 is special for Z^8)
  ok   E8 shells of norm 2n, n = 1, 2, 3: [240, 2160, 6720] = 240 sigma_3(n)
  ok   identity (not a test): (8 pi^4/3) / zeta(4) = 240, so 240 sigma_3(n) = (8 pi^4/3) n^3 times sigma_3(n)/(zeta(4) n^3)
  ok   identity (not a test): pi^2 n times (8/pi^2) sigma(n)/n = 8 sigma(n) = r_4(n) for odd n (the densities are asserted, not computed here)
  NUMERICAL Ingham: n in [20000, 20400): D(n) / ((6/pi^2) sigma(n) ln^2 n) has mean 1.061, min 0.696, max 1.236 (lower-order terms in ln n); correlation of D(n)/n with sigma(n)/n: 0.9788
  ok   NUMERICAL illustration of Ingham's theorem (CITED): D(n)/n follows sigma(n)/n (correlation above 0.9 on the window; the lower-order terms in ln n depend on n through other divisor sums)
